{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-14-1","title":"Isaiah 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God's merciful restoration of Israel. 3 Their triumphant exultation over Babel. 24 God's purpose against Assyria. 29 Palestina is threatened.</p>\n<p>the Lord. 40:1,2; 44:21,22; 54:7,8; Le 26:40-45; De 4:29-31; Ne 1:8,9 Ps 98:3; 102:13; 136:10-24; 143:12; Jer 50:4-6,17-20,33 Jer 51:4-6,34-37; Lu 1:54,72-74 choose. 27:6; Zec 1:17; 2:12 set. De 30:3-5; Jer 24:6,7; 29:14; 30:18-22; 31:8-12; 32:37-41 Eze 36:24-28; 39:25-29 the strangers. 19:24,25; 49:16-23; 56:6-8; 60:3-5; 66:20; Ru 1:14-18; Es 8:17 Jer 12:15,16; Zec 2:11; 8:22,23; Mal 1:11; Lu 2:32; Ac 15:14-17 Eph 2:12-19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-2","title":"Isaiah 14:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>and the house. 18:7; 60:9-12; 61:5; Ezr 2:65; Ro 15:27; 2Co 8:4,5; Ga 5:13 and they. Ps 68:18; 2Co 10:5; Eph 4:8 whose captives they were. Heb. that had taken them captives.they shall rule over. 60:14; Jer 30:16; Da 7:18,25-27; Zec 14:2,3; Re 3:9; 11:11-18 Re 18:20-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-3","title":"Isaiah 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>12:1; 32:18; De 28:48,65-68; Ezr 9:8,9; Jer 30:10; 46:27,28; 50:34 Eze 28:24; Zec 8:2,8; Re 18:20; 19:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-4","title":"Isaiah 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>proverb. or, taunting speech. Jer 24:9; Eze 5:15; Hab 2:6 How. 6,17; 47:5; 49:26; 51:23; Jer 25:9-14; 27:6,7; 50:22,23 Jer 51:20-24,34,35; Da 7:19-25; Hab 1:2-10; 2:6-12,17 Re 13:15-17; 16:5,6; 17:6; 18:5-8,20 golden city. or, exactress of gold. 13:19; 45:2,3; 2Ch 36:18; La 4:1; Da 2:38; Re 18:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-5","title":"Isaiah 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>29; 9:4; 10:5; Ps 125:3; Jer 48:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-6","title":"Isaiah 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>who smote. 33:1; 47:6; 2Ch 36:17; Jer 25:9; Da 7:19-21; Jas 2:13 continual stroke. Heb. a stroke without removing. ispersecuted. 13:14-18; 21:1-10; 47:1-15; Jer 25:26; 50:31; Re 17:16,17; 18:8-10 and none. 46:10,11; Job 9:13; Pr 21:30; Da 4:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-7","title":"Isaiah 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>they. 49:13; Ps 96:11-13; 98:7-9; 126:1-3; Pr 11:10; Jer 51:48; Re 18:20 Re 19:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-8","title":"Isaiah 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>55:12,13; Eze 31:16; Zec 11:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-9","title":"Isaiah 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Hell. or, The grave. from. Pr 15:24 is moved. Eze 32:21-32 chief ones. Heb. leaders, or, great goats. Jer 50:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-10","title":"Isaiah 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Art thou also. Ps 49:6-14,20; 82:6,7; Ec 2:16; Lu 16:20-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-11","title":"Isaiah 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>pomp. 21:4,5; 22:2; Job 21:11-15; Eze 26:13; 32:19,20; Da 5:1-4,25-30 Am 6:3-7; Re 18:11-19 the worm. 66:24; Job 17:13,14; 24:19,20; Mr 9:43-48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-12","title":"Isaiah 14:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>How art thou fallen. 13:10; 34:4; Eze 28:13-17; Lu 10:18; 2Pe 2:4; Re 12:7-10 Lucifer. or, day-star. 2Pe 1:19; Re 2:28; 22:16 weaken. 4-6; Jer 50:23; 51:20-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-13","title":"Isaiah 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>thou. 47:7-10; Eze 27:3; 28:2; 29:3; Da 4:30,31; Zep 2:15; Re 18:7,8 I will ascend. Eze 28:9,12-16; Da 8:10-12 the mount. 2:2; Ps 48:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-14","title":"Isaiah 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>ascend. 37:23,24 I will be. 47:8; Ge 3:5; 2Th 2:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-15","title":"Isaiah 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>thou. 3-11; Eze 28:8,9; Mt 11:23; Ac 12:22,23; Re 19:20 to the. Eze 32:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-16","title":"Isaiah 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>shall narrowly. Ps 58:10,11; 64:9 Is this. 4,5; Ps 52:7; Jer 50:23; 51:20-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-17","title":"Isaiah 14:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>made. 13:19-22; 64:10; Eze 6:14; Joe 2:3; Zep 2:13,14 opened not the house of his prisoners. or, did not let hisprisoners loose homewards. 45:13; 58:6; 2Ch 28:8-15; Ezr 1:2-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-18","title":"Isaiah 14:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>all of. 22:16; 2Ch 24:16,25; Ec 6:3; Eze 32:18-32 house. Job 30:23; Ec 12:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-19","title":"Isaiah 14:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>thou.The prophet having briefly set forth, in the beginning of this chapter, the deliverance of Judah from captivity, in consequence of the destruction of Babylon, then introduces this triumphant song, the beauties of which are excellently illustrated by Bp. Lowth.</p>\n<p>1Ki 21:19,24; 2Ki 9:25,34-36; Jer 8:1,2; 16:6; 22:19 go. Jer 41:7,9; Eze 32:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-20","title":"Isaiah 14:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>the seed. 13:15-19; Job 18:16,19; Ps 21:10; 37:28; 109:13; 137:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-21","title":"Isaiah 14:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>slaughter. Ex 20:5; Le 26:39; Mt 23:35 do not. 27:6; Hab 2:8-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-22","title":"Isaiah 14:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>I will. 13:5; 21:9; 43:14; 47:9-14; Jer 50:26,27,29-35; 51:3,4,56,57 the name. Job 18:16-19; Pr 10:7; Jer 51:62-64 remnant. 1Ki 14:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-23","title":"Isaiah 14:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>make. 13:21,22; 34:11-15; Jer 50:39,40; 51:42,43; Zep 2:14; Re 14:8 Re 18:2,21-23 I will sweep. 1Ki 14:10; 2Ki 21:13; Jer 51:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-24","title":"Isaiah 14:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Lord. Ex 17:16; Ps 110:4; Jer 44:26; Am 8:7; Heb 4:3; 6:16-18 Surely. 46:10,11; Job 23:13; Ps 33:10; 92:5; Pr 19:21; 21:30; Jer 23:20 Jer 29:11; La 3:37; Mt 11:25; Ac 4:28; Eph 1:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-25","title":"Isaiah 14:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>I will. 9:4; 10:16-19,32-34; 17:12-14; 30:30-33; 31:8,9; 37:36-38 Eze 39:4 then. 5; 10:24-27; Na 1:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-26","title":"Isaiah 14:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>5:25; Zep 3:6-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-27","title":"Isaiah 14:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>the Lord. 23:9; 43:13; 46:11; Job 40:8; Jer 4:28; 51:59; Ro 8:28,31 his. 9:12; 2Ch 20:6; Job 9:12; 23:13; Ps 33:11; Pr 19:21; 21:30 Da 4:31-35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-28","title":"Isaiah 14:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>A.M. 3278. B.C. 726. 6:1; 2Ki 16:20; 2Ch 28:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-29","title":"Isaiah 14:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Rejoice. Pr 24:17; Eze 26:2; 35:15; Ho 9:1; Ob 1:12; Mic 7:8; Zep 3:11 whole. Jos 13:3; 1Sa 6:17,18 because. 2Ch 26:6; 28:18 for. 2Ki 18:8 cockatrice. or, adder. 11:8 a fiery. 30:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-30","title":"Isaiah 14:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>the firstborn. Job 18:13 the poor. 5:17; 7:21,22; 30:23,24; 33:16; 37:30; 65:13,14 and I. Jer 47:1-7; Eze 25:15-17; Joe 3:4-8; Am 1:6-8; Zep 2:4-7 Zec 9:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-31","title":"Isaiah 14:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Howl. 13:6; 16:7 for. 20:1; Jer 1:14; 25:16-20 none shall be alone. or, he shall not be alone. appointedtimes. or, assemblies.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-14-32","title":"Isaiah 14:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>shall one. 39:1; 2Sa 8:10; 2Ki 20:12-19 the Lord. 12:6; 37:32; Ps 87:1,5; 102:16,28; 132:13,14; Mt 16:18 and the. 11:4; 25:4; Zep 3:12; Zec 11:7,11; Jas 2:5 trust in it. or, betake themselves unto it. Pr 18:10; Mt 24:15,16; Heb 12:22</p>"}]}